  "title": "Erdős Problem #33",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $A\\subset\\mathbb{N}$ be such that every large integer can be written as $n^2+a$ for some $a\\in A$ and $n\\geq 0$. What is the smallest possible value of $ \\limsup \\frac{\\lvert A\\cap\\{1,\\ldots,N\\}\\rvert}{N^{1/2}}? $ Is $ \\liminf \\frac{\\lvert A\\cap\\{1,\\ldots,N\\}\\rvert}{N^{1/2}}>1? $ ",
